        <mxCell id="fRQu4YJESxOBhfQmVjDm-14" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="AM (Amplitude Modulation) is the process of changing a Carrier signal&#39;s amplitude over time using another signal (Modulator).&amp;nbsp;&lt;div&gt;If the Modulator Signal is periodic and in audio range (&amp;gt; 20 hz), we will hear so called side bands, which are simple additions and subtractions of multiples of both frequencies.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;In AM, the Carrier Signal is audible&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
