        <mxCell id="fRQu4YJESxOBhfQmVjDm-43" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="FM (Frequency Modulation) is the process of changing a carrier signal&#39;s frequency over time with another signal (Modulator). If the Modulator Signal is periodic and in audio range (&amp;gt; 20 hz), we will hear so called side bands – additional frequencies (which are additions and subtractions of multiples of both frequencies.) Important here is that the spectrum changes according to the amplitude of the Modulator -&amp;gt; the higher the amplitude, the higher the overones is the spectrum ()so called INDEX)&amp;nbsp;" vertex="1">
